      "reasoning": "NBRC1020 and NBRC824 both print Na2SeO3 4 mg and Na2WO4 4 mg; the hydrate forms are unspecified. NBRC1020 supplies 1 L distilled water; NBRC824 omits the Se/W solvent/preparation denominator. Both receiving media use 1 mL. The NBRC824 denominator cannot be borrowed from NBRC1020 or the receiving medium. NBRC1020 and JCM317 have the same nominal listed masses (4 mg sodium selenite and 4 mg tungstate reagent) plus 1 L distilled water, but NBRC1020 omits hydrate qualifiers while JCM317 explicitly states Na2WO4·2H2O. Omission establishes neither anhydrous identity nor equality/difference. Keep these source-bound partial proposals; do not merge or co-install them as proved-distinct owners without source-applicable supplied-reagent evidence or an explicitly reviewed common nominal scope. The 1 L is added water, not a demonstrated final solution volume.",
