      "disposition": "new_distinct_ingredient_proposal",
      "reasoning": "JCM1425 explicitly references JCM317 Se/W solution and uses a 1.0 mL receiving dose. JCM317 specifies Na2SeO3 4 mg, Na2WO4·2H2O 4 mg and 1 L distilled water. NBRC1020 and JCM317 have the same nominal listed masses (4 mg sodium selenite and 4 mg tungstate reagent) plus 1 L distilled water, but NBRC1020 omits hydrate qualifiers while JCM317 explicitly states Na2WO4·2H2O. Omission establishes neither anhydrous identity nor equality/difference. Keep these source-bound partial proposals; do not merge or co-install them as proved-distinct owners without source-applicable supplied-reagent evidence or an explicitly reviewed common nominal scope. The 1 L is added water, not a demonstrated final solution volume. The retained new_distinct_ingredient_proposal disposition is the historical proposal-workflow category, not evidence of chemical disjointness; current merge and proved-distinct co-installation are withheld. Previously recorded JCM852 lower amounts/hydrated selenite and JCM431 alkaline-formula comparisons are unchanged; they do not establish a difference from the NBRC preparation.",
      "applicability": "Reviewed every one of the 1 original occurrences and complete frozen recipe objects. The following occurrence_bindings retain exact labels, nested/root location, original amount and source IDs; primary claims apply only to their explicit recipe/stock chain. The case-level native occurrence count is not replaced with any helper constant.",
