      ],
      "description": "This exact source preparation uses8.4gNaHCO3 with100mLwater,CO2saturation andsealedautoclaving. The original amount iswateradded,notanexplicitmake-uptofinal100mL. Generic84g/Lstock owner and its J451autoclavedunderCO2context do not establish identical finalvolume or priorCO2saturation. A distinct source-defined operational identity preserves these facts rather than silentlymergingbyrounded1Mmolarity. NBRC1257 and NBRC1321 both specify 8.4 g NaHCO3 plus 100 mL distilled water, CO2 saturation and autoclaving in tightly sealed CO2-filled bottles. The source qualification and complete preparation establish the same stock; neither source states make-up to a final 100 mL. Bicarbonate solution*** is a source-local footnote pointer with no strength, sodium specification or CO2 preparation in the token. It is not a standalone identity-bearing name for this particular stock, so preserve its exact REJECTED_LABEL/source entry and its positive occurrence-level assignment. This is a per-string applicability judgment, not export convenience or rejection of bicarbonate as a material. Bicarbonate solution (1.0 M)*** states a nominal strength but still requires the *** footnote to identify the sodium salt, added-water preparation and CO2 saturation. Preserve its exact REJECTED_LABEL/source entry as a non-name for this specific owner and retain its positive source-occurrence assignment. Nominal strength alone is not full formulation. Neither bicarbonate token has an established competing preferred owner in the checked scope; no SUPPRESS action is justified.",
